{"t": 1794112943.31136, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fees-float", "files": [{"content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n\n\ndef fee(amount: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Processing fee: 1% of the amount, rounded to cents.\n\n    Rounding is done on the exact decimal value with ROUND_HALF_UP, per the\n    card-network contract (PAY-88): binary float rounding is not acceptable.\n    \"\"\"\n    value = Decimal(str(amount)) * Decimal(\"0.01\") * 100\n    return float(value.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n", "path": "payments/fees.py"}], "message": "Round fees half-up on exact decimal values\n\nfee() used binary float rounding, so exact-decimal values like 2.675\nrounded down to 2.67. Compute on Decimal(str(amount)) and quantize with\nROUND_HALF_UP to honour the card-network contract (PAY-88).\n\nFixes the failing contract-tests check on PR #214.", "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
